      <h2> Fact 2: Lightning Strikes</h2>
      <p> Lightning strikes the Earth about 100 times every single second That is roughly 8
    millions lightning strikes per day!</p>
      
      <h3>How hot is lightning?</h3>
      <p>A single bolt of lightning is around 30,000 Kelvin - five times hotter than the surface
    of the Sun.</p>

       
      <h4>Can lightning strike twice?</h4>
      <p>Yes! Lightning absolutely can and does strike the same place more than once, especially
  tall structures like towers and tress.</p>

